I don't have your current `PlantsList.jsx` file — it hasn't been shared in this conversation. Could you paste it so I can make the exact edit you're describing? I want to make sure I preserve your existing status-clear logic, `confirmingId` handling, focus behavior, and `aria-live` setup rather than guessing at the implementation.

In the meantime, here's the core technique I'll apply once I see your file:

```jsx
// A counter that increments on every status update, even if the message is the same.
// Appending an invisible character tied to the counter forces the live region
// to re-announce, because the DOM text content actually changes.

const [statusCount, setStatusCount] = useState(0);
const [statusMsg, setStatusMsg] = useState('');

const announce = (msg) => {
  setStatusMsg(msg);
  setStatusCount(c => c + 1);
};

// In the JSX:
<p role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
  {statusMsg}
  {/* Invisible counter forces the browser to treat repeated text as a new announcement */}
  <span className="sr-only">{` (${statusCount})`}</span>
</p>
```

The `sr-only` span (visually hidden, still in the DOM) means the rendered text changes every time even when `statusMsg` is identical, which makes screen readers re-announce it. The `statusCount` value is only heard if the user navigates to it manually, and even then it's unobtrusive.

Paste your file and I'll weave this in, keeping everything else untouched.
